cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use ScaleRank, please cite it as below."
title: "ScaleRank: dimensionality reduction that preserves neighbour ranks over a range of scales"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Tsuji
    given-names: Shingo
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0234-9519"
abstract: >-
  ScaleRank makes maps you can read at every scale: the neighbourhoods inside
  each cluster, and how the clusters sit relative to each other. It preserves
  neighbour ranks over a range of neighbourhood sizes K, sampled with
  probability proportional to K^-gamma, without N x N structures, and has an
  optional densMAP-style density term. Rust core with a Python package
  (scalerank on PyPI).
keywords:
  - dimensionality reduction
  - visualisation
  - embedding
  - single-cell
license: BSD-3-Clause
repository-code: "https://github.com/tsjshg/scalerank"
url: "https://tsjshg.github.io/scalerank-web/"
version: 0.1.1
date-released: "2026-11-23"
